Have you ever wondered how apps like Swiggy, Blinkit and Zepto get their data so fast?

Change your location and the entire home page changes almost instantly.

Even things already in your cart can suddenly show as unavailable if that store can't deliver to your new location.

How is all of this happening so quickly?

There’s probably a lot going on behind the scenes: location-based inventory, APIs, caching, databases and real-time updates, all working together.

We use these apps every day, but it's pretty crazy when you actually stop and think about the backend powering them.

Now I'm curious: how would you design a system like this?

